# ---- macOS ----
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# ---- Windows ----
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- Editor / IDE ----
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---- AI assistants and coding agents ----
# Contributors use assistants; their configuration, caches and transcripts are working
# files, not part of the record. Nothing here has ever been tracked, so this is a guard
# rather than a cleanup. Using a tool that is not listed means adding it here in the
# same PR.
.claude/*
# .claude/settings.json is deliberately NOT ignored, for the same reason as the lockfile
# below: it is shared, reviewable project configuration, and this repo commits the things
# that would otherwise change what runs with no diff. settings.local.json is personal and
# stays out. The directory has to be written .claude/* for this negation to work at all:
# git will not look inside an excluded directory to reconsider a path.
!.claude/settings.json
CLAUDE.local.md
claude_mcp.json
.cursor/
.cursorrules
.cursorignore
.windsurf*
.cline*
.roo*
.aider*
.agent/
.agents/
.openai/
.llmignore
chatgpt.json
openai.json
gemini.json
deepseek.json
kimi.json
tomb.json
# Context packagers: a flattened copy of the repo, which goes stale the moment it is
# written and is regenerated on demand anyway.
repomix-output.txt
llm-context.txt
codebase-summary.md

# ---- Node (server-side only: the functions under api/, never the site itself) ----
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
# package-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored. Vercel installs the api/ dependencies
# on every build, so without a lockfile it re-resolves them each time and a new release
# of a dependency can change what runs in production with no commit and no diff. This
# repo's whole premise is that CI rebuilds and fails on any drift; the lockfile is what
# extends that to the one thing the build does not generate itself.
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# ---- Vercel ----
.vercel
.vercel.json.local

# ---- Environment / secrets ----
# .env* covers .env, .env.local and .env.production alike. The negation has to stay last:
# git only reconsiders an excluded path if a later rule re-includes it.
secrets.*
.env*

# ---- Stray local-preview symlinks (serve.py needs none; guard against old ones) ----
app/assets
app/data
app/robots.txt
app/sitemap.xml

# ---- Logs / temp ----
*.log
tmp/
.cache/

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc